                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Very nice lil adventure game!\r\n\r\nDef a must play if u like Uncharted, Indiana Jones or the good Tomb raider games (you know the ones with actual tomb raiding..)\r\n\r\nIts like a much shorter indie version of those games minus the action\r\n\r\n+ Very nice puzzles (only few of them were kinda weird/boring, while the rest are great)\r\n- A very few puzzles could have been reworked to be better (i.e. the early 4 disc puzzle could have given us an actual puzzle instead of just placing the 4 discs, each into 1 slot)\r\n+ Great progression, nice amount of everything from story related \"mundane\" things to exploring ruins and puzzle solving\r\n+- Sadly its kinda short (unless you get super stuck somewhere u'll beat it in 3-4h), even tho you do explore a lot of locations so it doesn't feel as short.. Either way, would have loved if it was longer (just expanding the correct selection of the levels/sections would have made it longer and better without feeling like its dragging on)\r\n+ Great story, nothing new or revolutionary, but fits the adventure tone perfectly!\r\n+ Beautiful locations\r\n+ Nice chars (obv its a bit dated as its a remake of older games so you don't have that many chars, but honestly its great)\r\n+- As the game is an older game remade sometimes the transition from 1 scene/area/\"gameplay\" into the other feels a bit \"fast\" like it could have given us 2more mins of playtime or something to better connect\r\n+ Very nice graphics\r\n+ Nice final boss (altho they could have made it overall a bit better/harder)\r\n+ Very nice ending, altho they should have added a min or two to make the ending feel more \"finished\"\r\n\r\nWould love if a game like this got a good budget for a new game as it could have the potential to be an amazing adventure game/series (I wouldn't expect this to be a new/next Uncharted, but hey if done right it could get close to games like Uncharted and welp getting close would be an huge achievement of its own!)",
